  "summary": "AgentScope is a Python agent framework (requires Python 3.11+) whose SDK exposes building blocks such as a ReAct loop, Toolkit, Model, Context, Event System, Permission & HITL, Middleware, Memory, and Workspace/Sandbox, plus a FastAPI-based agent service with a Web UI. Contributor-facing rules (Conventional Commits, lazy imports, pre-commit/pytest, responsible AI use) are documented in CONTRIBUTING_zh.md. Evidence coverage: 151 of 201 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
